[ ] Trial a persistent nvim server on devbox instead of shpool for the facilitator =nvim-server $Darrion, 2026-10-20: the facilitator runs in a sidekick terminal inside nvim, so closing nvim ends the session. Idea: a systemd user unit runs nvim --headless --listen on a socket; attach with nvim --remote-ui --server <socket>, leave with :detach, reattach from desktop or phone. Checked on devbox: NVIM v0.12.5, :detach exists. To find out in the trial: whether two clients can attach at once, how the terminal resizes between phone and desktop, how nv (\$NVIM) behaves, and whether shpool is still needed for plain shells. Owner here because chezmoi carries the devbox units and nvim config.$ !2 ^2026-10-20T07:07 #01a15823-3125-7053-bc20-0232bbfa8cd3
[ ] Bring cargo and uv tools under chezmoi, locked =locked-installers $Darrion, 2026-10-21: chezmoi stays the one manager for user-level tools, preferring pacman, then pinned release binaries, then installers with locks. About 30 long-tail tools today: 9 externals, 5 npm (pinned, tree unlocked), about 8 cargo and 4 uv (unpinned). Cargo tools with release binaries become externals (cargo-binstall may help find the URL; the external keeps our sha256). npm gets a committed package.json and lock, installed with npm ci --ignore-scripts. uv tools get a uv pip compile constraints file and --no-build; check whether uv tool install enforces hashes.$ ^2026-10-21T01:16 #01a15c08-65b7-7d80-93f5-4339716e9aa4
[ ] Add an on-demand bump command for chezmoi pins =pin-bump $Run by hand, matching on-demand upgrades: for each external, ask GitHub for the latest release and its published sha256 digest, rewrite version and checksum together, and regenerate the npm and uv locks, so one diff shows everything an upgrade brings in. Deterministic, no tokens.$ ^2026-10-21T01:16 <locked-installers #01a15c08-65c1-7820-825c-caf29bd4f06b
