[ ] An nvim view to pick a landing, read its review note and record a verdict with a key =verdict-picker $Moved from agent-sandbox on 2026-10-25 (Darrion: the nvim view is for them, so it lives in chezmoi; the CLI stays in agent-sandbox). The view calls the CLI and plain git, never reads \$AGENT_RUNS itself: 'agent-verdict --pending' for the list, 'git notes --ref=review show' for the note, 'agent-verdict <id> --agree|--disagree' to record. pick a workspace from 'agent-verdict --pending', load its refs/notes/review into quickfix (and offer :DiffviewOpen on the landed range), then agree or disagree with a key, calling agent-verdict. One layer at a time: wait for Darrion to use the completion first. Open: where it lives (agent-sandbox share/nvim, or Darrion's nvim config).$ !2 ^2026-10-25T18:08 #01a1743f-a1d4-7b60-b347-c86fd6046286
